---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---
<LegalPage
  title="Disclaimer | AccessBell"
  heading="Disclaimer"
  description="Important information about the limits of automated accessibility testing and the AccessBell website accessibility checker. Not legal advice."
  path="/disclaimer"
  updated="2026-09-28"
>
  <h2>Not legal advice</h2>
  <p>
    The information on accessbell.co, including scan results, reports, blog articles and any other content, is provided for general informational purposes only. It is not legal advice and does not create an attorney-client relationship. Accessibility law differs by country, state and sector and changes over time. For advice about your specific obligations, consult a qualified attorney.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits of automated testing</h2>
  <p>
    The AccessBell website accessibility checker uses automated rules to detect common barriers based on the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG). Automated testing can identify many objective, code-level issues, but it cannot evaluate every WCAG success criterion. Some requirements, such as whether alternative text is meaningful, whether focus order is logical or whether captions are accurate, require human judgment.
  </p>
  <p>
    A scan result, score or report from AccessBell does not certify that a website is accessible or that it complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act, Section 508, the European Accessibility Act, EN 301 549, AODA or any other law or standard. A page with no detected issues may still contain barriers.
  </p>

  <h2>No guarantee against claims</h2>
  <p>
    Using AccessBell does not guarantee that you will not receive a demand letter, complaint or lawsuit. We recommend combining automated monitoring with manual testing by people familiar with assistive technology, and feedback from users with disabilities.
  </p>

  <h2>AI-assisted suggestions</h2>
  <p>
    Suggested fixes, including those generated with the help of machine learning, are drafts. They may be incomplete or incorrect for your context and must be reviewed by a qualified person before being applied.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party content and links</h2>
  <p>
    Our website links to external sites and references third-party standards and legislation for convenience. We are not responsible for the content, accuracy or availability of external sites. Dates and requirements described in our content were accurate to the best of our knowledge at the time of writing and may have changed since.
  </p>

  <h2>Scanning websites you do not own</h2>
  <p>
    You should only scan websites you own or have permission to test. Our checker requests a single public page in the same way a browser does, but you are responsible for how you use the results. See our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this disclaimer can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or through our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
